"explanation": "Taluma is the age-grade passage that marks a young person's move from helper to responsible herder. It is held at the end of the summer plateau stay, once the household has judged the adolescent ready. Completing it formally transfers charge of a set portion of the household flock during the seasonal moves between valley and plateau. That is its main institutional consequence. It does not settle marriage, since kin groups negotiate those arrangements separately and on their own timetable. It also does not give a seat or voice in the grazing council, which depends on household headship and other routes. Nor does it assign the ledger, because the household's senior keeper holds that work. Taluma changes herd duty and little else, and informal esteem follows from that.",
